authors				Daniel Veillard, Nick Wellnhofer and libxml2 contributors
status				testing

headline			XML C parser and toolkit
description
	Libxml2 is the XML C parser and toolkit developed for the GNOME project.  This build is the one libsyllable's os::XML is built on: the parser, serialization, XPath 1.0, DTD validation, W3C XML Schemas and Relax-NG, without threads, iconv, zlib or HTML.
licenses			MIT

home				gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2
locations			https://download.gnome.org/sources/libxml2/2.15/

; The CMake build (cmake/Ports.cmake, libxml2_static) builds this port with
; patches/Makefile and patches/config.h in place of configure, and
; patches/include/libxml/xmlversion.h (the features os::XML uses): one static
; library of PIC objects, linked into libsyllable with its symbols kept
; private.  It is not installed on the boot volume.
make-file			Makefile

documentation		README.md Copyright NEWS
